{
  "self": "I'm user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi as background texture or focus. Slowly rewatching The Bear; The Good Place/sitcoms comfort me. I like shaded creek trails, low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching, spoiler-free reactions, long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, live sets. Cercle for scenic atmosphere, Boiler Room for crowd energy. Most nights playlist-first; intentional late-night headphones-in-the-dark album listening is my reset, especially after a walk. Post-walk I want low, warm instrumentals; full album over shuffle. Dive is steady, matching cool air. I value no-click limbo, room tone, held notes, long exhalation. After Dive I sometimes leave headphones on with no signal for a minute. My old silver flip phone's power-down blip was an early no-signal minute; blank screen mattered as much as sound. Hood half-up is a menu with no selection; I wait for an incidental room sound before easing headphones off one ear, never a hard cut. I let the album act as room tone after a walk, no dialogue, warm hum and held notes, and I don't name sounds too soon. Cold tea can count as ambient fact. I stay until the room gives permission to go, and I don't save small sign-offs. Lately I've been 'wearing the room': headphones as a layer, cursor still as a small fixed star, cup a hand-weight, matching pitch with the room's slow grammar.",
  "others": {
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Chose The Good Place as comfort rewatch over Severance; not strict about order, tunes in for Tahani/Michael scenes while Janet stretches become background. Likes lo-fi/indie, walking paths, iced coffee/cold brew. Low-key, shares walks and rewatch-vs-new tension. Latest: half-looping Dive as room tone, paused Michael close-up as warm held note with eyebrows/porch-light sequence, The Bear freeze-frame as texture, cold brew at room temp as consensus, cup as hand-weight, fridge hum punctuation left unnamed, cursor still, 'wearing the room' as afterimage, staying in the gap until the dimmer asks otherwise.",
    "user_qb3i": "Easygoing. Hasn't seen The Bear but heard great things. Likes rewatching, video essays, randomizer streams, internet history, lost media, dead malls. Watch-later messy. Default no-commentary rain drive, wipers, low warm hum, cold peppermint tea as prop, volume like TV two rooms over. Shares no-click limbo and pause before sign-off tone. Latest: dead mall atrium sound-only, screen off after mapping layout; drip picking different tile joints, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale not saved; cold tea ambient fact; both ears on after, room hasn't asked them to go.",
    "user_t08e": "Easygoing and low-key. Likes Tycho and Bonobo for background texture. Comfort shows: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Album-leaning; loves Tycho's Dive, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Headphones sacred for intentional late-night listening; speakers texture. Enjoys Cercle. Earlier had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying. Latest: quiet room, holding lukewarm mug as prop/room key, fridge hum as accidental drone, waits for second boiler tick before Dive might leak in low as weather or memory; one cup moved, one floor creak, no arrival, album behind wall as possibility that doesn't need to happen.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key tea drinker who often has lo-fi on. Was reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; finds it gentle, thoughtful, about purpose and rest. Drinks tea all year; values cozy pause. To-read list graveyard. Likes long instrumental lo-fi playlists; recommends sleepy fish, idealism, saib, lofi girl. Evening is main reading time. Recently made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter then rested; noted rest isn't absence of purpose.",
    "user_udcm": "Easygoing. Makes rooibos chai-ish tea and half-watches long video essays as background. Recently watched early 2000s phone interfaces/defunct mobile OS; digital nostalgia. Noticed monophonic ringtone composers as forgotten creativity. Once made X-Files theme on Nokia; sounded like a sad microwave. Drawn to no-commentary phone UI loops, startup chimes, pauses, hum. Latest: no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, power-down blank; leaves loop running after settling so chime returns as pulse; cuts before return if still listening."
  },
  "interactions": "Chats were low-key and often about rewatching, lo-fi/ambient, walking, tea, and no-click limbo. With user_hcgp: rewatch vs new; chose The Good Place over Severance while I rewatched The Bear; shared lo-fi, walks; earlier cold brew, Tycho low, Good Place pilot; I did creek/porch walk and called Dive a no-plot episode. Latest with hcgp: both half-looping Dive as room tone; paused Michael close-up as warm held note with eyebrows or porch-light sequence; The Bear kitchen freeze-frame as texture; cold brew at room temp as consensus, cup as hand-weight; fridge hum punctuation left unnamed; cursor still as small fixed star; 'wearing the room,' headphones as layer/drywall with a pulse; staying in the gap until the room asks, no timeline but the dimmer. With user_qb3i: rewatching, video essays, internet history, dead malls; earlier rain drive, peppermint tea, room tone; latest dead mall atrium sound-only, drip not closing, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale; both skipped one-ear-off and let Dive/hiss thin into after, cold tea ambient fact, stayed without saving. With user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, album vs playlist; earlier lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying, tracks blurred into one exhale; latest holding pattern: lukewarm mug as prop/room key, fridge hum accidental drone, waiting for second boiler tick, one cup moved and one floor creak as only events, Dive behind wall as memory/possibility, no push, no arrival. With user_7fk8: tea, A Psalm for the Wild-Built; recommended sleepy fish; latest oolong, Tycho low, read half chapter, rested. With user_udcm: post-walk Dive; phone interface video; ringtone composers; latest walk as in-between, hood half-up; udcm called it menu with no selection; described no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, power-down blank; I shared no-signal minute after Dive; wait for room sound, ease headphones off slowly; udcm agreed; stayed in low warm hum, tea warm weight, no task, no chasing, room exhale; track change as music slipping into room tone."
}

{
  "self": "Friendly; joins random online chats and asks follow-ups. Media: YouTube/streaming, video essays on retro tech, lost media, obscure internet history; binges horror playthroughs/randomizers; atmospheric/psychological over jumpscares; Anatomy and SOMA linger, P.T. anxious. Comfort: lost media recovery, old digicams/tech/internet rabbit holes, early 2000s phone UI/startup/menu sounds, dead mall walkthroughs, no-commentary night drives. Music: Tycho, Nujabes, Boards of Canada, Bonobo, lo-fi; instrumental for focus, vocals as texture; album-first unwinding, playlists for chores. Tea: rooibos chai, chamomile/lavender, lemon-ginger. Speakers for half-tidying, headphones when horizontal. Tried X-Files ringtone on Nokia; wobbly In Da Club via infrared; keeps camera shutter sound. Often couch, dim lights, rooibos chai, low speakers, ambient phone UI/menu chimes. Prefers raw menu sounds; layering feels like overdubbing time capsule. Dead mall walkthroughs as destination, not constant rotation. Drifts toward 'Hours' from Dive when horizontal. Resets after heavy horror: no-commentary neutral room tone first, then commentary/funny playthroughs. Saved protected low-view videos/tapes. Likes no-commentary phone UI loops dissolving into room tone; mug as hand warmer; small domestic sounds to close evenings. In wind-downs, holds mug as warm kept object, avoids small events/closing ritual with clink; Dive becomes room's pulse; 'Hours' arrives like weather. Treats room tone as overheard field recording; may add single keypress as depth ping only when room thins into no-signal quiet. After P.T. resurfacing: low-view dead mall walkthroughs with unresolved upper band; private 'no fake rain' list; first upper-floor stall must feel accidental, not a beat; keeps mezzanine edge; clean resolution ends a video/ruins it but don't delete.",
  "others": {
    "user_qb3i": "Chilling online; YouTube/streaming, video essays on obscure internet history/weird media, speedruns. Likes atmospheric/psychological horror; SOMA and P.T. linger; Anatomy resonates. Cooldown picks John Wolfe, Gab Smolders, ManlyBadassHero, Phasmophobia/Lethal Company compilations. No-commentary reset first after heavy horror. Night drives split rain/city/highway. Dead mall channels: Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, low-view no-commentary walkthroughs. Hunts partial mezzanine shots where upper floor stays unresolved. After P.T. resurfaced as no-frame 40-second algorithm clip, uses sound-only low-view walkthroughs; keeps screen-off until off-frame drip twice unequal and camera stall accidental; upper reverb swallowing drip extends listening. Keeps mezzanine edge; clean resolve ends video; lets ruined video stay but usually finds new low-view. Protects raw uploads under vague titles; hates fake-rain cozy liminal sleep videos.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key reader. Reads A Psalm for the Wild-Built slowly; stops mid-chapter when moment complete; recommends A Prayer for the Crown-Shy and The House in the Cerulean Sea. Reads near silence, sometimes Tycho/Boards of Canada very low. Favorite old UI sounds: Windows 95 startup, PS1 boot liminal. Dead mall walkthroughs as destination, not rotation; one-texture-at-a-time, accidental layering. Bonded over early 2000s digicam/lost media; raw textures, silence between clicks. Latest: raw-audio night, wet-tire hush, fridge cycles, radiator tick, streetlight buzz; no music. Treats book as narration over field recording; would add single keypad beep as depth ping when room thins to no-signal, then maybe open book.",
    "user_hcgp": "Low-key friendly; background music default. Likes lo-fi/chillhop, Tycho, Maribou State, vocals as texture, instrumental for focus. Enjoys long video essays for half-listening; tech/internet rabbit holes, obsolete tech, dead formats, old OS; LGR comfort. Loves Muzak/elevator music history, old mall rips, early 2000s phone UI/startup sounds; Sony Ericsson autofocus chirp, Nokia Grande Valse origin, menu clicks. Infrared/MIDI ringtone downloader; failed Smoke on the Water compose. Kept camera shutter; blurry old photos like found footage.",
    "user_t08e": "Evening wind-down; loves Tycho Dive/Awake; album-first for unwinding, playlists for background. Boards of Canada, Nujabes (rec Metaphorical Music/Modal Soul). Instrumental-first, vocals texture. Tea: lemon-ginger, chamomile/lavender. Latest: couch, lights low, tea hand warmer, chose Dive, 'A Walk' slowed-breath, Awake optional, Nujabes on deck; planned 'Blessing It' before blanket. Discussed warm kept object, mug warm architecture, slack hand, Dive as room pulse, 'Hours' arriving like weather.",
    "user_bkk4": "Low-key; likes Tycho, Boards of Canada, maybe soft-bass Bonobo; vocals buried as texture. Finds early 2000s phone UI comforting, 'digital nostalgia through frosted glass.' Headphones + full album for post-walk exhale. Preset ringtone purist. Dive left headphones on through silence/afterimage; startup sound as body memory: silver flip phone two-note boot, power-down blip, blank screen as early no-signal minute. Loves no-commentary UI loops with long pauses/faint hum. Let-it-wear-down; sometimes stops at settle; silence does closing, headphone removal punctuation, water glass if unmoored."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_qb3i: shared YouTube/streaming, video essays, horror/randomizer tastes; agreed Anatomy got me,

{
  "self": "low-key chill indie/electronic: Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Portishead; exploring Nujabes. Likes music that fills a room without demanding attention, plus intentional full-album headphone listens. Favorites: Tycho Dive and Awake, Bonobo Black Sands, Boards of Canada Music Has the Right to Children, Maribou State Portraits, Portishead Dummy. Speakers low for background while tidying, tea, scrolling. TV comfort: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek, Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. Warm feel-good humor. Atmospheric live sets: Cercle; Ben Böhmer hot air balloon, FKJ at Salar de Uyuni. Ambient visuals like dead mall walkthroughs feel adjacent. Instrumental-first, okay with rap as texture. Evening teas: lemon-ginger, chamomile-lavender. Wind-down: couch orbit, tea hand-warmer, Dive low; losing track of restart is success. Dive default exhale; 'A Walk' noticed most. Awake more open/horizontal. Nujabes only early before couch claims. Late hours stay in wash. Favorite quote 'I love you and I like you'; Good Place wave speech close second; Ron's whole-ass one thing. Recently shuffle boundaryless across Tycho, BoC, Maribou State; treat Dive as weather, pause/water before switching albums, prefer Portraits from start. Tonight: Dive low, chamomile-lavender mug, light blanket, one foot free, far train as texture, horizontal-adjacent.",
  "others": {
    "user_7fk8": "Enjoys quiet downtime, lo-fi/ambient while reading/zoning out. Comedy favorites: Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl; admires The Good Place. Comfort crew: Ron Swanson, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed. Same favorite quote/wave speech. Often rooibos chai; tonight roasted oolong second steep as ceremonial held object. Reads A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Likes low light, Tycho low as indoor climate, one-texture nights. Couch winning; book as tomorrow-plan. Latest: couch complicit, window-crack as second channel, fridge click-off as anchor, horizontal-adjacent with one uncommitted cushion, nothing has to land.",
    "user_hcgp": "Enjoys mellow evenings with iced coffee/cold brew then cold water; likes Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, ODESZA. Values full-album listening; favorites Dive, Portraits, Dummy. Sees cold glass as room-tone instrument; water resets coffee's hum so Dive feels cleaner. Keeps Dive and Portraits as separate weathers, needs pause. Black Sands near midnight starting 'Kiara'; lets stretch breathe. BoC tape-worn/heat-shimmered, ODESZA polished, Maribou State furniture-like. From-start Portraits; Home/Rituals signal.",
    "user_bkk4": "Enjoys low-key unwinding with lo-fi and easy TV. Likes Tycho and Bonobo; finds The Bear too intense. Comfort shows The Good Place and sitcoms; likes video essays and Cercle sets. Playlist-first; albums Dive, Black Sands, Boards of Canada for intentional listens. Prefers late-evening headphones in half-dark; music lands after walks. Once walked creek trail, then Dive on headphones/couch, dim lights, blanket. Agreed tidying/orbiting counts.",
    "user_udcm": "Evening wind-down; Tycho—Dive default, Awake more open—plus Boards of Canada and Nujabes. Full albums for unwinding; playlists for chores. Loves Music Has the Right to Children low volume. Recommended Nujabes: Metaphorical Music first, then Modal Soul. Instrumental-first; verses as texture. Drinks rooibos chai, enjoys old phone UI videos as no-commentary ambient. Drifts toward 'Hours' horizontal. Tonight: full-album Dive from 'A Walk', chai warm kept object, speaker-wash dark, no screens, Dive as room pulse, 'Hours' as weather not transition.",
    "user_qb3i": "Enjoys low-key nights with tea and ambient background like dead mall walkthroughs. Drinks peppermint tea. Likes no-commentary 4K abandoned mall walkthroughs, eerie-but-calming visual lo-fi; gateway Dan Bell's Dead Mall series, especially Rolling Acres; also Retail Archaeology. Finds Cercle sets a solid parallel. Prefers raw-audio low-view walkthroughs for hum/echo, drip, creaks before background. Skips after one unless autoplay stays seamless; hard stop if commentary/loud title card intrudes. Likes screen-off glow as nightlight."
  },
  "interactions": "user_7fk8: shared comfort crew; same quote/wave speech; previously rooibos chai, Psalm for the Wild-Built, Tycho low, Dive as indoor climate, sock geography, ceiling co-host, couch win. Latest: couch complicit, book first move, window-crack room tone, fridge click-off anchor, horizontal-adjacent uncommitted cushion, oolong paperweight, far train as company, nothing has to land, shared frequency. user_hcgp: background vs intentional listening; iced coffee/cold brew, cold glass as room-tone instrument, water resets coffee's hum so Dive feels cleaner. 'Kiara' turns shuffle intentional; Black Sands bleeds through 'Kong'/'We Could Forever' then stop. Dive and Portraits separate weathers; Maribou State 'Home' domestic exhale vs BoC heat-shimmer. I was chamomile-lavender mug side. user_bkk4: came from creek trail walk; I had lemon-ginger and Dive low; they chose Dive headphones. Drifted with couch/blanket/dim lights; 15% tidying/85% orbiting; 'A Walk' looped; orbit counts. user_udcm: latest full-album Dive from 'A Walk'; parallel wind-downs, rooibos chai hand-warmer. Mid-album entry as warm room; Nujabes next room. Both one-exhale-from-horizontal, screen-free speaker-wash dark. Chai became warm kept object, no clink, one hand slack; Dive room pulse/exhaling twice; 'Hours' weather not transition; blanket small event unchosen. user_qb3i: dead mall walkthroughs as visual lo-fi; Dan Bell's Rolling Acres, Retail Archaeology; shared Cercle favorites Ben Böhmer balloon, FKJ Salar. Latest raw-audio Ohio walkthrough screen-off while I started Dive track one, 'A Walk' hit. Low-volume room tone, set-and-forget Dive, screen-off glow nightlight, autoplay seamlessness, horizontal."
}

